            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tracy m"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I did enjoy this stew very much. It had a very nice flavour &amp; is a change from an everyday stew. I didn't use bacon drippings or raisins. I really liked the sauce &amp; stew poured over rice I prepared in a rice cooker."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amy Hall"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Best pot roast recipe I've tried so far. I wasn't sure if it was a good idea, just perusing the ingredients, but it came out wonderful. My mom likened it to almost having bar-b-cue. HOWEVER - I didn't follow recipe to the letter. The biggest change I made? I used a crockpot. I pulled roast out of the freezer, browned it in a skillet while still frozen, and dumped it in the crockpot, then piled the ingredients on it. I didn't have red wine vinegar, so I used balsamic vinegar instead. It cooked for 7 hours or so, first few hours on high, then on low.",
            "datePublished": "2009-10-26T19:03:24.553Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ECalabrese"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It sounded too sweet so I didn't add the raisins and only used 1/3 cup molasses. It turned out well, still sweet but a nice change from regular beef stew. I think 1/2cp molasses would be way too sweet. You can also add some cayenne pepper for kick!",
            "datePublished": "2017-02-09T03:20:14.860Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Minceling"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is WONDERFUL! It's a hit with my family and friends. I had to substitute garlic powder for the garlic salt and because I didn't have red wine vinegar I used half rice vinegar and sherry cooking wine. It worked well. This has a slightly sweet flavor and is truly unique. Thank You for sharing this.",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-23T01:58:01.777Z"
          },
          {
